@hanickadot, thank you for a great project! I've heard about it for years and finally got the chance to try it 🤗 

I was looking to implement a RegEx-based parser for my [`less_slow.cpp` tutorial](https://github.com/ashvardanian/less_slow.cpp), where I need to find all matches of a multi-line pattern in a byte-string. I've noticed, that some of the aspects of the documentation were outdated, and @bortsov has opened a related issue with a proposed patch.

---

I've also noticed an issue with an end-of-line symbol, but haven't localized the issue yet. Here is what my usage pattern looks like:

```cpp
void config_parse_ctre(std::string_view config_text, std::vector<std::pair<std::string, std::string>> &settings) {
    for (auto match : ctre::multiline_search_all<R"(^\s*([^#:\s]+)\s*:\s*([^#:\s]+)\s*$)">(config_text)) {
        std::string_view key = match.get<1>().to_view();
        std::string_view value = match.get<2>().to_view();
        settings.emplace_back(key, value);
    }
}
```

This RagEx pattern works fine with `std::regex`, but `ctre::` seems to have troubles with the dollar sign in the end. Please let me know if you have any ideas, or if I should open an issue.

